what The cold run of this lap reads seed_link RED, and the root is the instrument rather than a page. inseed() walks UP from a link target looking for an allowed ancestor, which is the right question for a FILE and the wrong one for a ROOM: template-manifest.bron allows context/ twenty-one named pages and never the directory, so the seed makes context/ to hold them while no allow row says context. Bisected across this tree's own history before claiming -- the ratchet crossed 820 to 821 at 757d59171e, petrichor's Members key, whose one new site is context/README.md -> ./, a page linking to the directory the seed made to hold it. The repair is one clause in the awk: after the upward walk fails, a target is in-seed when an allow row names a file beneath it. Measured on a patched copy before claiming: 821 to 820, exactly one site cleared, zero front-door links moved, no page edited and no ceiling lowered. The control gains a second pen builder whose manifest allows one FILE under deep/ rather than the room, proving both sides in one tree -- the own-room link free and unlisted, an empty-room link still counted and named -- plus a mutation that strikes the clause out of a copy of the scan and counts the carried room again; 25 legs to 30, each named in the witness. AND IT IS COORDINATION RATHER THAN ONLY REPAIR: petrichor's live claim opens the same Members key on three more front doors, each carrying the same ./ link, so without this clause that lap lands three more sites on a ratchet already over its ceiling. Touches no module source, no page, no ledger row and no roster row.
